CDialogTree
{
Name=The Crypt's Fronts
Portrait=!None
Should Have Voiceovers=0
Default Canceled Node Action=
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 rear passage
Text=This is the corridor the garrison falls back through: scuffed flagstones, a wedge of broken shield, and a door that has been forced from the far side more than once.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 rear barred
Text=The bar drops into its brackets. Whatever comes up this passage now will have to come through the door, and the door has held before.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 stone door
Text=A stone door stands open on its counterweights, and the dust on the sill has been walked through in both directions.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 stone bolted
Text=The counterweight drops and the stone seats itself. The horde will have to take the long way round to reach the retreat, and the long way is where the knights are.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 protect walls
Text=Thirteen low walls stand between this gallery and a single coffin at the back of it, and every one of them was raised in a hurry by somebody who expected to be overrun.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 walls opened
Text=The walls grind back. The way to the last coffin is open, and so is the way to it from the galleries -- the garrison will not be able to hold this room again.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 the three crypts
Text=Three sealed crypts, and a switch. Somebody has scratched a warning beside it in a hand that had time to be careful.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 crypts opened
Text=The three lids come up together. Whatever the garrison was keeping in here is loose in the corridors now, and it is not on their side.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=3 tide holding
Text=The line is where it was. Neither side has gained a yard since you came down here.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=3 tide garrison
Text=The horde's routes into the upper galleries are shut. The garrison is holding more ground than it was when you arrived.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=3 tide necromancer
Text=The garrison's ground is thinner than it was when you arrived, and what you did in the corridors is why.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=4 freed in good order
Text=The knights go out like lamps, in order, from the corridors you shut first. The last one to go is standing at a fire that has given no heat for two hundred years, and he stops counting.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=4 freed into a ruin
Text=The knights go out like lamps, and what is left holding the corridors is the thing they were holding them against. You have freed a garrison out of a crypt you made worse, and both of those are true at once.
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=4 freed from a stalemate
Text=The knights go out like lamps, all at once, mid-step, and the horde in the lower galleries has nothing left to push against. The siege does not end. It simply stops having two sides.
Should Have Voiceover=0
}
